# DuckDB's own signed builds of the extensions MacPorts does not build into
# the library, one subport each, installed where the library looks for them
# (EXTENSION_DIRECTORIES below). A MacPorts build of an extension would be
# unsigned, which DuckDB refuses to load, so these are DuckDB's binaries,
# fetched per version and architecture.
#
# DuckDB's known extensions not built into duckdb, by the names DuckDB
# publishes them under, except motherduck, whose licence is not stated, and
# odbc_scanner, which links Homebrew's unixODBC by absolute path. Each entry
# holds the extension's own version (a commit, read from the file), an
# optional license (MIT by default), the extensions it loads at start
# (depends), notes, and the checksums of each platform DuckDB publishes it
# for, which sets the subport's supported_archs. DuckDB can republish an
# extension at the same URL after a release; extension-checksums.py --check
# reports it.
# Each bundles its dependencies statically; mysql_scanner and spatial carry
# LGPL code (libmariadb, GEOS). Regenerate the checksums for a new version
# with extension-checksums.py.
set extension_dir   ${prefix}/lib/duckdb/extensions
